    "summary": "<p><strong><a href=\"https://thoughts.hmmz.org/2026-05-31.html\">The solution might be cancelling my AI subscription</a></strong></p> I find this post by David Wilson very relatable. David lists 16+ projects he's spun up with AI tooling, and concludes:</p> <blockquote> <p>I didn't mean to build most of these things. Usually the Claude session started with something like \"<em>write a quick script for X</em>\", and one hour later the result is not a <em>quick script for X</em>, nor in the usual case is my problem solved, whatever the original itch happened to be.</p> <p>On that last point, this technology is <strong>horrific</strong> for attention. It's a thermonuclear ADHD amplifier and I have seen the same effect in every single one of my adult friends. Folk running 3 screens simultaneousl...",
